WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.026 --> 00:00:02.151
I'm on the date right
now, we're on the rooftop-

00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:03.992
(hisses)

00:00:03.992 --> 00:00:05.325
Stop doing that!

00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:11.614
So today I'm going on a
blind date with a vampire.

00:00:11.614 --> 00:00:13.692
I'm Anthony Montemarano, I'm part of a,

00:00:13.692 --> 00:00:16.205
I guess you'd say clan or a
coven called the Sabretooth Clan

00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:20.139
Father Sebastian is a
fang-smith, he made these for me.

00:00:20.139 --> 00:00:23.612
My only experience with
vampires is watching Twilight.

00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:25.613
I only watched the first two movies

00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:27.341
because the second one
was shit, let's be real.

00:00:27.341 --> 00:00:29.547
You get a name that relates to something

00:00:29.547 --> 00:00:32.043
that you do in life, mine was Onius.

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:34.650
Onius is like a gatherer of people,

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.958
it also says that Onius drinks wine,

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.211
so I was like yeah, that sounds like me.

00:00:39.211 --> 00:00:41.323
Oh my goodness, I don't know
anything about vampires.

00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:43.550
I mean I know that they
drink pretty girls' blood,

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.924
so, I mean, hey.

00:00:44.924 --> 00:00:46.652
Choosing to be a vampire,
I guess you'd say

00:00:46.652 --> 00:00:47.868
is like a value system.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:49.916
I'm not really trying to
be immortal for a guy,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.998
so if that's what he's
expecting on the first date,

00:00:51.998 --> 00:00:53.308
it's not gonna happen.

00:00:53.308 --> 00:00:56.235
Most of the people I've dated
are non-vampires, I guess.

00:00:56.235 --> 00:00:59.947
I'm a very opposites attract kinda guy.

00:00:59.947 --> 00:01:02.197
I'm not Bella, I'm sorry.

00:01:04.422 --> 00:01:05.255
I'm Anthony.

00:01:05.255 --> 00:01:06.684
I'm Selorm, nice to meet you.

00:01:06.684 --> 00:01:07.836
Selorm, cool.

00:01:07.836 --> 00:01:09.773
That's an interesting name,
love it, love the hair.

00:01:09.773 --> 00:01:10.989
Anthony, I like your hair, too.

00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:12.252
Yeah, I'm excited to do this.

00:01:12.252 --> 00:01:13.786
I don't know what we're
going to be doing, but

00:01:13.786 --> 00:01:14.619
I'm sure it'll be fun.

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:15.883
Actually, we're going to be going to

00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:17.530
the Museum of Death and then we'll have

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.851
an Italian place down the
street called Fabiolus Cucina.

00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:22.394
And have some dinner
there and finish her off

00:01:22.394 --> 00:01:26.074
here at the building on the
top of the roof with some wine.

00:01:26.074 --> 00:01:28.506
Mm, vampires are romantic,
okay, let's do it.

00:01:28.506 --> 00:01:30.876
So we started the date by
going to the Museum of Death.

00:01:30.876 --> 00:01:32.877
I was really excited
because I kind of have

00:01:32.877 --> 00:01:34.524
a small fascination with death.

00:01:34.524 --> 00:01:36.555
I was excited to go in, but it was a lot.

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:38.138
Just went in the Museum of Death.

00:01:38.138 --> 00:01:39.452
Can't show it on camera.

00:01:39.452 --> 00:01:41.179
Museum of Death was interesting.

00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:42.682
Pictures of serial killers and
the victims they had slain.

00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:45.532
There were real pictures
of bodies inside of there.

00:01:45.532 --> 00:01:48.378
The informative things
that were cool was like

00:01:48.378 --> 00:01:50.586
the mortician's side of the autopsies

00:01:50.586 --> 00:01:52.218
that were performed and how they did it.

00:01:52.218 --> 00:01:54.300
So it was a lot especially for a date.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.899
I'd say it's worth checking out, but

00:01:55.899 --> 00:01:57.965
it's definitely a lot to read and see.

00:01:57.965 --> 00:01:59.565
We're heading to the restaurant now.

00:01:59.565 --> 00:02:01.195
All right, so I have questions.

00:02:01.195 --> 00:02:02.028
Yeah.

00:02:02.028 --> 00:02:03.691
What kind of music do you do?

00:02:03.691 --> 00:02:05.500
A couple of bands,
one's called Neon Coven.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.970
C-O-V-E-N.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.682
Kind of like electronic dance rock.

00:02:08.682 --> 00:02:11.004
The other one's called Mursick,
it's kind of an opera rock.

00:02:11.004 --> 00:02:12.778
It's actually kind of
vampire rock in a way.

00:02:12.778 --> 00:02:14.635
I don't think I've heard opera rock.

00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:17.114
Like Transylvania and
like, back in the old times

00:02:17.114 --> 00:02:19.196
in movies when you hear
all the organ playing

00:02:19.196 --> 00:02:21.945
when there's vampires and
like, it's very gothic.

00:02:21.945 --> 00:02:23.275
Do you have any pets?

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:25.724
I have three gargoyles in my room.

00:02:25.724 --> 00:02:28.474
(crickets chirp)

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.532
Pets, man, I have a dog, no gargoyles.

00:02:41.532 --> 00:02:43.452
Do you talk to them, do you feed them?

00:02:43.452 --> 00:02:45.086
No, I just keep air brushing them.

00:02:45.086 --> 00:02:46.844
I paint their nails.
Oh, that's sweet.

00:02:46.844 --> 00:02:49.101
We're about to walk into Fabiolus.

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:50.991
Vampire's favorite restaurant.

00:02:50.991 --> 00:02:52.655
A lot of garlic, so I gotta be careful.

00:02:52.655 --> 00:02:54.302
Unfortunately I love it so they gave me

00:02:54.302 --> 00:02:55.932
this pill that I can take.

00:02:55.932 --> 00:02:57.549
It's like Lactaid for garlic.

00:02:57.549 --> 00:02:59.915
It's dinner time so he
has to take out his fangs.

00:02:59.915 --> 00:03:01.244
I gotta take these out because

00:03:01.244 --> 00:03:03.804
I don't want to swallow them on accident.

00:03:03.804 --> 00:03:04.943
Whoa.

00:03:04.943 --> 00:03:06.492
(laughs)
Oh my god.

00:03:06.492 --> 00:03:07.998
Wait, so what are you gonna eat?

00:03:07.998 --> 00:03:10.029
As long as you're not trying
to drink my blood, I'm happy.

00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:11.535
So do you sleep in the day time?

00:03:11.535 --> 00:03:13.519
I actually do sleep in a lot.

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:15.358
I work for myself and I have like,

00:03:15.358 --> 00:03:17.052
my room is very blacked out.

00:03:17.052 --> 00:03:19.629
I am this close to actually
sleeping in a coffin.

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:21.228
And I actually do have a basement.

00:03:21.228 --> 00:03:22.206
(high pitched tone)

00:03:22.206 --> 00:03:23.806
We got our wonderful dinner.

00:03:23.806 --> 00:03:26.302
Steak, of course it's rare
because he loves blood.

00:03:26.302 --> 00:03:27.757
(laughter)

00:03:27.757 --> 00:03:30.300
And you have, here is
the special of the night

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.770
is the handmade gnocchi pesto with shrimp.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.845
Pesto is made from basil,
Parmesan, olive oil,

00:03:36.845 --> 00:03:39.934
and pine nuts, oh there's
garlic in it, too, obviously.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.871
I left that out because I'm a vampire.

00:03:41.871 --> 00:03:43.791
No, I don't die from garlic.

00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:47.038
So we just finished
dinner, it was really good.

00:03:47.038 --> 00:03:48.510
Amazing pesto.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.029
He got a lot of garlic today,

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.757
I was worried about him but he survived.

00:03:51.757 --> 00:03:54.765
Fortunately the wine counteracts
the effects of garlic.

00:03:54.765 --> 00:03:57.278
What has been your
fascination with vampires?

00:03:57.278 --> 00:03:59.681
Honestly I just don't
believe that they exist.

00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:01.921
Or that they're real, I
used to hope they didn't.

00:04:01.921 --> 00:04:04.123
I've never seen one, and yet here you are.

00:04:04.123 --> 00:04:05.019
Here I am.

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:06.895
Do you usually tell everybody
that you're a vampire?

00:04:06.895 --> 00:04:08.414
I kind of stay low key with it.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.804
What vampire really means to me,

00:04:09.804 --> 00:04:12.812
is that the music I
write is very gothic and

00:04:12.812 --> 00:04:15.565
was inspired by vampire-esque films.

00:04:15.565 --> 00:04:17.421
My love of Tim Burton films.

00:04:17.421 --> 00:04:18.974
He kind of gave me a really good window

00:04:18.974 --> 00:04:21.313
into like the world of vampires, you know.

00:04:21.313 --> 00:04:23.489
They're people just like you and me.

00:04:23.489 --> 00:04:24.670
Just with fake fangs.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.742
The rooftop was really nice,
we had a view of Los Angeles.

00:04:27.742 --> 00:04:29.423
- [Anthony] Really nice chairs.

00:04:29.423 --> 00:04:32.139
And so it kind of just was
a great way to end the date.

00:04:32.139 --> 00:04:33.089
Was I a good date?

00:04:33.089 --> 00:04:35.340
(laughter)
I've heard that before.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.645
Oh no, you were great.
Okay.

00:04:37.645 --> 00:04:39.343
You were super fun.
You're super fun!

00:04:39.343 --> 00:04:41.229
You have great energy and
that's what's important.

00:04:41.229 --> 00:04:43.393
The date tonight was super
fun, I had a great time.

00:04:43.393 --> 00:04:45.999
Selorm was a great person,
we had a lot in common.

00:04:45.999 --> 00:04:48.065
She's very intrigued by
the whole vampire culture.

00:04:48.065 --> 00:04:50.443
Hanging out with Anthony
was kind of an eye opener.

00:04:50.443 --> 00:04:52.938
It kind of exposed me
to the fact that this is

00:04:52.938 --> 00:04:54.733
really just a community
of people that have

00:04:54.733 --> 00:04:56.321
a lot of similar interests.

00:04:56.321 --> 00:04:58.061
I think this has really
enhanced my interest

00:04:58.061 --> 00:04:59.594
in vampire culture.

00:04:59.594 --> 00:05:01.517
First blind date I went on with a vampire

00:05:01.517 --> 00:05:03.646
and it was great, he's
a really cool person.

00:05:03.646 --> 00:05:05.357
Maybe I'll even get my own pair of fangs.

00:05:05.357 --> 00:05:07.274
You will.
Second date.

00:05:07.274 --> 00:05:09.278
Second date.
Getting fangs.

00:05:09.278 --> 00:05:10.111
Totally.

00:05:11.498 --> 00:05:13.915
(calm music)

